/*****************************************************************************
    THE MECHANISM: incant/iterT1m walks a small tree with two mutually
    recursive iterators, walkA and walkB, each iterating the node the other
    handed it.

    WHAT IS WRONG: nothing is wrong with the walk any more -- it now visits
    every node exactly once, which is the right answer. What is wrong is that
    both things the fleet pins for it still describe the OLD BROKEN walk, in
    which leaves were revisited and a refusal was announced seven times. So the
    fleet reports two reds against a fixture that is behaving correctly, and it
    has done so for long enough that nobody remembers which side is stale.

    THE FIX WANTED: look at the two comparisons this file prints, and either
    bless the new walk and re-pin both baselines, or say why the old walk was
    right and the new one is a regression. It is one decision, not two: both
    rows moved for the same reason.

    HOW TO USE THIS FILE: run it. It defines the same two iterators, walks the
    same tree, and prints measured beside pinned for both rows. The anchor
    fixIterT1mHere is an inert assignment at the point where the two answers sit
    side by side -- set a breakpoint conditioned on that name to step into the
    comparison with the numbers already on screen.

    Footnote: pop.sh rows "iterT1m (mutual recursion: KNOWN WRONG, pinned)" and
    "iterT1m announces its refusal 7 times"; baselines genLadder/iterT1m.divergence
    and the grep for aCTionIterate: source. docs/knownErrors.md KE-4.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(FixIterT1m);
define
    leafA   i j;
    leafB   k l;
    trunk   leafA leafB;
    fixIterT1mHere=0;
    fxRows=0;

    walkA argument code={
        fxRows = fxRows + 1;
        print "A " taG argument:;
        iterate grup on argument;
        while ++grup
            walkB(grup);
        };

    walkB argument code={
        fxRows = fxRows + 1;
        print "B " taG argument:;
        iterate grup on argument;
        while ++grup
            walkA(grup);
        };

    fxRun code={
        cerr "== fixit iterT1m -- the live walk, then measured beside pinned ==":;
        cerr "-- the walk as it runs TODAY (each line is one visit) --":;
        walkA(trunk);
        cerr :;
        cerr "ROW 1  the walk itself":;
        cerr "   pinned   14 visits -- leafA, leafB, i, j, k and l each seen TWICE":;
        cerr "            (genLadder/iterT1m.divergence, the mutual-recursion bug)":;
        cerr "   measured " fxRows " visits -- every node exactly once":;
        cerr "ROW 2  the refusal announcement":;
        cerr "   pinned   7 lines of `aCTionIterate: source` on stderr":;
        cerr "   measured 0 -- the refusal this counted no longer happens":;
        cerr :;
        cerr "   Both rows moved because the walk stopped revisiting. Bless it and":;
        cerr "   re-pin, or name why the old answer was the right one.":;
        fixIterT1mHere = 0;
        cerr "ANCHOR fixIterT1mHere -- both answers are on screen above":;
        cerr "FIXIT iterT1m SENTINEL -- reached the end":;
        stop();
        };
    ;
fxRun();
